{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788177919,"nonce":"JQCmBjBXxFQ6f+zz/4STDghQrbY=","message":"RECON LANDED — decompiled-source sweep for this spec, orchestrator session 6,\nBORGES. Full report is handed to the worker at dispatch; the load-bearing\nfindings are here so they are on the issue rather than only in a scratch file.\nEvery claim below was re-verified by the orchestrator in the tree, at the line\ngiven.\n\n**Namespace correction to this spec's body.** `Bill.cs`, `BillStack.cs` and\n`BillUtility.cs` are under `RimWorld/`, not `Verse/`. The body's `Verse/Bill.cs`\ncitations are wrong; the members are right.\n\n**`BillStack.AddBill` really is four lines and validates NOTHING** (BillStack.cs\n:69-73 — `bill.billStack = this; bills.Add(bill);`). Confirmed by reading it.\nThis is the whole reason the spec exists, so the gate to reproduce is now exact:\n\n- recipe present in `def.AllRecipes`\n- `RecipeDef.AvailableNow`\n- `RecipeDef.AvailableOnNow(table)` — the UI's own filter, `ITab_Bills.cs:86`\n- `BillStack.Count \u003c 15` — enforced in `BillStack.DoListing:141`. Note the UI\n  hardcodes the literal rather than its own `MaxCount = 15` (BillStack.cs:15).\n\nThe mechanitor and skill-range dialogs are ADVISORY — vanilla adds the bill\nanyway. Do not turn those into refusals; report them, do not enforce them.\n\n**`AvailableNow` is a write-on-read and WorldSafe does NOT yet cover it.**\nIt bottoms out in `ResearchProjectDef.IsFinished` -\u003e `ResearchManager.GetProgress`,\nwhich inserts a zero entry into the scribed `progress` dictionary on a miss —\nthe same trap 2.4 catalogued. `WorldSafe.Finished(ResearchProjectDef)` is the\nguarded route and is shipped, but there is no recipe-level equivalent. So this\nspec OWES `WorldSafe.RecipeAvailableNow(RecipeDef)`, re-deriving `AvailableNow`\nover `WorldSafe.Finished` instead of the raw getter. Adding it to WorldSafe (not\nto a new file) keeps one catalogue.\n\n**The storage-group shadowing trap is REAL**, verified: `Building_Storage\n.GetStoreSettings()` returns `storageGroup.GetStoreSettings()` when\n`storageGroup != null` (Building_Storage.cs:100-107), so writing `.settings`\ndirectly while grouped edits a shadowed object. `Zone_Stockpile` cannot be\ngrouped, so the trap is building-only.\n\n**`StorageSettings.Priority`'s setter is where haul invalidation lives** — and\nit skips all of it when `ProgramState != Playing`. Always go through the\nproperty, never the backing field.\n\n**`SetStoreMode(mode, group)` is mandatory, not a convenience** — `storeMode`\nand `storeGroup` are private. It only log-errors on a mode/group mismatch and\nstores the values regardless, so validate before calling or you author a red\nerror, which breaches the zero-red-errors invariant.\n\n**`Reorder` checks only the lower bound** (confirmed): moving the last bill down\nthrows out of `List.Insert`, and a bill not in the stack gets inserted as a\nforeigner at `offset \u003e= 1`. The acceptance line about `bad-args` rather than a\nthrow is therefore load-bearing, not decorative.\n\n**NEW HAZARD, and it is in DESIGN's decisions log now (4177df6): write-on-SAVE.**\n`Bill.ExposeData` narrows the live `ingredientFilter` of every bill whose recipe\nhas a `fixedIngredientFilter`, during the SAVING pass, as a side effect of\nwriting the file. It only removes allowances and converges after one save. Two\nconsequences: an autosave can change a bill's reported filter with no player\naction, and — the reason it is in DESIGN — \"save the game and read the Scribe\nXML\", which sessions 2.2 and 2.4 used as the independent second reader, is NOT\nindependent for this surface. Prove filter behaviour with a live read plus a\ngame-acted change instead.\n\n`Bill_Production.ShouldDoNow`'s three scribed `paused` writes were re-verified\nand match what `WorldSafe.BillState` already routes around. No `Rand.*` anywhere\nin the bill or storage neighbourhood; the only RNG hazard nearby is the\ninherited `Zone.Cells` shuffle, for which `WorldSafe.ZoneCells` is the route.","files":null}]}